\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Specification curve for $\varphi _{\text  {overseer}}$ at medium granularity. Upper panel: claim class against specification rank, classes ordered by frequency, so each step's width is that class's share of the space. The dashed line marks the size-matched random null's modal share; the pooled comparison is confounded by circuit size, discussed in Section\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:null}. Lower panel: which analytic level is active for each specification. The solid band on the comprehensiveness row is the composition effect of the discard rule in Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:discard}; the seed rows are unstructured, which is the same result as seed removing 0.0009 from $F$ in Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:fixed}.\relax }}{8}{figure.caption.22}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:speccurve}{{1}{8}{Specification curve for $\varphi _{\text {overseer}}$ at medium granularity. Upper panel: claim class against specification rank, classes ordered by frequency, so each step's width is that class's share of the space. The dashed line marks the size-matched random null's modal share; the pooled comparison is confounded by circuit size, discussed in Section~\ref {sec:null}. Lower panel: which analytic level is active for each specification. The solid band on the comprehensiveness row is the composition effect of the discard rule in Table~\ref {tab:discard}; the seed rows are unstructured, which is the same result as seed removing 0.0009 from $F$ in Table~\ref {tab:fixed}.\relax }{figure.caption.22}{}}
